   Nagasawa, Satoi and Nakamura, Yuka and Kojima, Motohiro and Tsuchihara,
   Katsuya and Seki, Masahide and Kanai, Akinori and Matsubara, Daisuke and
   Kohno, Takashi and Noguchi, Masayuki and Nakaya, Akihiro and Tsuboi,
   Masahiro and Ishii, Genichiro and Suzuki, Yutaka and Suzuki, Ayako},
Title = {Spatially resolved gene expression profiling of tumor microenvironment
   reveals key steps of lung adenocarcinoma development},
Journal = {NATURE COMMUNICATIONS},
Year = {2024},
Volume = {15},
Number = {1},
Month = {DEC 6},
Abstract = {The interaction of tumor cells and their microenvironment is thought to
   be a key factor in tumor development. We present spatial RNA profiles
   obtained from 30 lung adenocarcinoma patients at the non-invasive and
   later invasive stages. We use spatial transcriptome sequencing data in
   conjunction with in situ RNA profiling to conduct higher resolution
   analyses. The detailed examination of each case, as well as the
   subsequent computational analyses based on the observed diverse
   profiles, reveals that significant changes in the phenotypic appearances
   of tumor cells are frequently associated with changes in immune cell
   features. The phenomenon coincides with the induction of a series of
   cellular expression programs that enable tumor cells to transform and
   break through the immune cell barrier, allowing them to progress
   further. The study shows how lung tumors develop through interaction in
   their microenvironments.},
